### Power of Three Problem Solution in Java

This problem can be solved using logarithms. We can use the property of logarithms that states `log(a^b) = b * log(a)`. If `n` is a power of `3`, then `log(n) / log(3)` should be an integer.

Here is a Java solution that uses this property:

```java
public class Solution {
    public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
        if (n <= 0) {
            return false;
        }
        double logN = Math.log(n) / Math.log(3);
        return Math.floor(logN) == logN;
    }
}
```

This solution works by first checking if `n` is less than or equal to 0. If it is, we return `false` because negative numbers and 0 cannot be powers of 3.

Next, we calculate the logarithm of `n` base 3 using `Math.log(n) / Math.log(3)`. If `n` is a power of 3, this will result in an integer.

Finally, we use `Math.floor(logN)` to get the integer part of the logarithm. If `logN` is an integer, then `Math.floor(logN)` will be equal to `logN`, and we return `true`. Otherwise, we return `false`.

